{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/951376-exalted-related-media-thunderbolt-fantasy-aka-exalted-the-tv-show","id":951376,"title":"[Exalted-related Media] \"Thunderbolt Fantasy\" aka Exalted the TV-Show","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-15T16:55:05-07:00","id":951376,"title":"[Exalted-related Media] \"Thunderbolt Fantasy\" aka Exalted the TV-Show","content":"We all knew that there was a bunch of badass puppeteers in Taiwan, of the non-hopping kind.<br /> They've been doing amazing work for the last several decades, making wuxia-puppetry. Now, Gen Urobuchi of<i> Fate/Zero</i> and <i>Puella Magi Madoka Magica </i>fame decided to work with the crowning jewel of that industry, to create a Puppet show for a new audience.<br /> <br /> AND IT IS GLORIOUS.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qvv1lkEu4vM\" data-code=\"qvv1lkEu4vM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/qvv1lkEu4vM/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> It's basically Exalted in a nutshell.<br /> It's got a Abyssal warlord in a shadowland manse, gathering the mightiest of daiklaves. Now, he is hunting the strongest of those, and is by pure &quot;accident&quot; opposed by a wandering Dawn Caste and a motley crew assembled by a dude mostly reminding me of a Sidereal.<br /> <br /> The fight scenes are amazingly choreographed, the costumes and aesthetics are everything I feel is lacking with modern fantasy anime to make a proper Exalted-feel. And all of this is made by filming hand-puppets. Freaking PUPPETS!<br /> <br /> Watch it. It's got 13 episodes, is on CrunchyRoll, and we're on episode 6.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>__________________________________________________ </b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><i>Preaching the enlightened gospels of Gaming Anarchy</i></b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/225-growls","name":"Growls","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T16:58:19-07:00","id":951380,"title":"","content":"Dang... Those are some REALLY awesome puppets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T17:14:56-07:00","id":951390,"title":"","content":"I think there is a special episode where they explain how they do this. It's a pretty amazing process.<br /> <br /> Also. I just realized that I can straight up use one of the &quot;heroes&quot; from the show as a Abyssal anti-hero. There's a character named Screaming Phoenix Killer, and he's straight out the best Dusk Caste I've seen in any media. Period. He is SO going into a campaign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>__________________________________________________ </b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><i>Preaching the enlightened gospels of Gaming Anarchy</i></b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/225-growls","name":"Growls","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T17:17:17-07:00","id":951392,"title":"","content":"Yeah, this show has been pretty incredible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T19:31:27-07:00","id":951444,"title":"","content":"Thunderbolt Fantasy is freaking <i>perfection</i>. It really does feel like a really good Exalted campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T19:37:50-07:00","id":951447,"title":"","content":"I just googled a video of it and was absolutely blow the eff away. That's freaking amazing!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T19:54:38-07:00","id":951456,"title":"","content":"I just ran through the first two episodes. And damn, this is pretty awesome.<br /> <br /> The fighting is really stylish and powerful, and the show wears the colors of its genre quite well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 08-15-2016, 10:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T02:08:13-07:00","id":951563,"title":"","content":"Currently, I'm trying to place castes or aspects on the characters.<br /> <br /> - Sh\u0101ng B\u00f9 Hu\u00e0n &quot;The Edgeless Blade&quot;<br /> He is pretty much a Dawn Caste who is not even the slightest bit impressed by all the crazy that is going on around him.<br /> <br /> - Gu\u01d0 Ni\u01ceo (Phantom Bird) <br /> Currently, I'm casting him as a Chosen of Secrets. And a very deceitful one at that, as the entire party (except our two other main characters) seem to know a bit more about his past.<br /> <br /> - D\u0101n F\u011bi (Vermillion Kingfisher) <br /> The scion of a dragonblooded lineage practicing Golden Jannisary style while protecting the ancient Ten-Thousand Years Daiklave &quot;Heavenly Punishment Blade&quot; from the greedy villains.<br /> <br /> - Ju\u01cen C\u00e1n Y\u00fan aka The Frozen Wonder<br /> The world most brazen Air Aspect with a lot to prove.<br /> And pretty good at the spear variant of Even Blade.<br /> <br /> - X\u00edng H\u00e0i aka Weeping Night<br /> She is to Necromancy what Mara is to Sorcery.<br /> Demon who hid in the real world.<br /> <br /> - Sh\u0101 W\u00fa Sh\u0113ng aka Screaming Phoenix Killer<br /> Dusk Caste. Period. Hell, even his clothes scream Abyssal. A total and utter Badass, and dual practioner of both Single Point Shining Into the Void and Steel Devil Style.<br /> <br /> - Sh\u00f2u Y\u00fan Xi\u0101o aka the Sharp-eyed Impaler <br /> I'm either partial to name him a Solar Archer supernal or a really good chosen of Mars.<br /> He's by far the best shot in the show.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>__________________________________________________ </b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><i>Preaching the enlightened gospels of Gaming Anarchy</i></b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/225-growls","name":"Growls","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T05:03:26-07:00","id":951608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Growls</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/951376-exalted-related-media-thunderbolt-fantasy-aka-exalted-the-tv-show?p=951563#post951563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Sh\u00f2u Y\u00fan Xi\u0101o aka the Sharp-eyed Impaler<br /> I'm either partial to name him a Solar Archer supernal or a really good chosen of Mars.<br /> He's by far the best shot in the show.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd go for Chosen of Mars - his signature &quot;shoot at where the target will be in about a minute&quot; seems right in a sidereal's wheelhouse.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12154-momerathe","name":"momerathe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12154_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T07:57:40-07:00","id":951713,"title":"","content":"I love this show dearly. Growing up, I used to watch quite a bit of wuxia movies and dramas with my parents. Now, I watch mostly anime because it's easier to get subs for them. But this is a glorious combination of dear childhood memories mixed with cool anime aesthetic with a hint of Chinese opera techniques mixed in. I love the soundtrack too, really enhances things.<br /> <br /> And I can't for when we get Sh\u0101ng B\u00f9 Hu\u00e0n and Gu\u01d0 Ni\u01ceo's poem read out. You know it's going to be a badass moment when that happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/723-talam","name":"Talam","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T19:44:01-07:00","id":952939,"title":"","content":"So aesthetically it looks right on the money for Exalted, but I'm having a hard time getting past the whole puppets thing. Does that get better? It looks really weird. It is super jarring for me. Am I going to get used to this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T02:35:57-07:00","id":953062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Childofthesun1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/951376-exalted-related-media-thunderbolt-fantasy-aka-exalted-the-tv-show?p=952939#post952939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So aesthetically it looks right on the money for Exalted, but I'm having a hard time getting past the whole puppets thing. Does that get better? It looks really weird. It is super jarring for me. Am I going to get used to this?</div> </div> </div> </div>You've seen episode 1 yet?<br /> Anyways, it's going to increase in style and amazing choreography. If you have a issue with the puppets? Just squint and pretend it's drawings.<br /> I got used to it after episode two, but different strokes you know.<br /> <br /> The story and the interaction between the characters picks up a lot after episode 4, mostly because of the presence of the Weeping Night","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>__________________________________________________ </b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><i>Preaching the enlightened gospels of Gaming Anarchy</i></b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/225-growls","name":"Growls","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T05:37:44-07:00","id":953111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Growls</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/951376-exalted-related-media-thunderbolt-fantasy-aka-exalted-the-tv-show?p=953062#post953062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You've seen episode 1 yet?<br /> Anyways, it's going to increase in style and amazing choreography. If you have a issue with the puppets? Just squint and pretend it's drawings.<br /> I got used to it after episode two, but different strokes you know.<br /> <br /> The story and the interaction between the characters picks up a lot after episode 4, mostly because of the presence of the Weeping Night</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nah I just watched the trailer. It hurt my eyes a little bit, in the &quot;I am completely unimmersed in this media because I can't forget that I'm watching some guys wave around some goofy puppets&quot; kind of way. I imagine this is how most people feel about anime. &quot;It's just a dumb cartoon.&quot; Getting used to it by episode two sounds good. I'll give it a shot.<br /> <br /> I think the part that bothers me most is the mouth and eyes. My brain just isn't processing that as a face yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T07:32:32-07:00","id":953157,"title":"","content":"One thing the show does a lot better than the opening credits, is giving narrative context to immerse yourself in.<br /> <br /> Once you learn about the story and watch a hour of it, I'm sure it'll be fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>__________________________________________________ </b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><i>Preaching the enlightened gospels of Gaming Anarchy</i></b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/225-growls","name":"Growls","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T16:59:31-07:00","id":953487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Growls</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/951376-exalted-related-media-thunderbolt-fantasy-aka-exalted-the-tv-show?p=953157#post953157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing the show does a lot better than the opening credits, is giving narrative context to immerse yourself in.<br /> <br /> Once you learn about the story and watch a hour of it, I'm sure it'll be fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. An hour in I'm totally immersed in the story, loving every second. But I really don't like the medium. Their lips never really move. It's like staring at dolls, and everyone thinks dolls are creepy.<br /> <br /> But th One-Eyed Implares introduction was SO COOL, and the samurai's intro in the first episode was dripping with, what, culture? The whole Buddha statue opening as a plot device was amazing.<br /> <br /> I say the samurai because I can't remember any names. Even organizations. Some translation is nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T17:38:11-07:00","id":953513,"title":"","content":"Well, maybe you'll learn to enjoy the silent horror? I never found dolls to be creepy. I'd say you can power through <br /> <br /> And in regards to names, I'd say you can use my previous list.<br /> I can add the rest of the names if you need them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>__________________________________________________ </b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><i>Preaching the enlightened gospels of Gaming Anarchy</i></b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/225-growls","name":"Growls","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T01:29:55-07:00","id":953715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Childofthesun1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/951376-exalted-related-media-thunderbolt-fantasy-aka-exalted-the-tv-show?p=953487#post953487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I say the samurai because I can't remember any names. Even organizations. Some translation is nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>The names are an issue. For sub reason the subs have the original (?) chinese names, which I can't even parse, and don't resemble the spoken Japanese (the Rot3K problem)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12154-momerathe","name":"momerathe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12154_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T14:57:30-07:00","id":958435,"title":"","content":"L\u01d0n Xu\u011b Y\u0101's soliloquy sure was a long time coming.<br /> <br /> I'm more and more curious about the exact form of Sh\u0101ng's true skills. It sounds like he may originally not even have used bladed weapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T23:54:51-07:00","id":958623,"title":"","content":"I find myself wondering why Asian historical fantasy has everyone looking like badass pimps while Western historical fantasy is twenty shades of brown leather.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T20:27:33-07:00","id":959047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/951376-exalted-related-media-thunderbolt-fantasy-aka-exalted-the-tv-show?p=958623#post958623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find myself wondering why Asian historical fantasy has everyone looking like badass pimps while Western historical fantasy is twenty shades of brown leather.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it has to do more with the fact that it's Wuxia than historical fantasy. I've watched Chinese and Korean historical fantasy shows before and they still have people in different shades of like brown and grey. It's just that Wuxia tends to be more fantastical, where you can have these flowing garments that would normally heavily interfere in a regular fight but just be a thing for these kinds of shows. Western historical fantasy tends to be a little more grounded, even if there are like wizards and dragons<br /> <br /> Now superheroes, superheroes get to be colourful and whacky in terms of costuming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/723-talam","name":"Talam","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T06:08:27-07:00","id":959196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/951376-exalted-related-media-thunderbolt-fantasy-aka-exalted-the-tv-show?p=959047#post959047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it has to do more with the fact that it's Wuxia than historical fantasy. I've watched Chinese and Korean historical fantasy shows before and they still have people in different shades of like brown and grey.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's a matter of cultural consciousness; people expect westerners to dress in leather a lot, because it's hard and tough and everyone is expected to be working all the time. Why they don't decorate or paint the leather, however, is not known to me.<br /> <br /> Us folks did actually wear a lot of stuff like that back in the day. Google 'hanfu' ('male hanfu' and 'female hanfu') and you'll see what I mean. They wore several layers in everyday life, and I imagine that whenever they needed to work or fight, they'd remove a few layers. What you see in shows like this is the equivalent of Neo fighting a hundred people in his hard leather priest coat.<br /> <br /> Finally, while I've definitely noticed that the last ten years of mainland Chinese TV is to really make the colors pop, no matter where and what the setting is, even the more muted, restrained shows of circa-2003 nor the old Shaw Brothers movies filmed on dusty Singaporean lots were what I'd call &quot;brown and drab.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11538,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11538-kingcrackers","user":"kingcrackers","date":". 08-28-2016, 09:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11538-kingcrackers","name":"kingcrackers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11538_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T06:54:00-07:00","id":959212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kingcrackers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/951376-exalted-related-media-thunderbolt-fantasy-aka-exalted-the-tv-show?p=959196#post959196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's a matter of cultural consciousness; people expect westerners to dress in leather a lot, because it's hard and tough and everyone is expected to be working all the time. Why they don't decorate or paint the leather, however, is not known to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, they did. Pretty much everything that could be decorated in the European middle ages was decorated; they loved their bling. Painted shields, banners, tabards, dyed fabrics were used basically everywhere they could be - and that's leaving aside the knights with their personal heraldry.<br /> <br /> Personally, I blame a) Hollywood and b) the concept of &quot;the dark ages&quot;. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12154-momerathe","name":"momerathe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12154_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T18:36:54-07:00","id":959607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/951376-exalted-related-media-thunderbolt-fantasy-aka-exalted-the-tv-show?p=959047#post959047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now superheroes, superheroes get to be colourful and whacky in terms of costuming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone needs to tell Zack Snyder this, stat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T19:09:27-07:00","id":959623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/951376-exalted-related-media-thunderbolt-fantasy-aka-exalted-the-tv-show?p=959607#post959607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Someone needs to tell Zack Snyder this, stat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, let's take a look at Wonder Woman. Admittedly her colours are darker than she should be but she's still sporting blue, red and gold. Even Superman has his blue and red, it's just kind of hard to see because Zack Snyder hates light or anything bright.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/723-talam","name":"Talam","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T16:42:06-07:00","id":962564,"title":"","content":"That was a pretty brutal episode, not just in terms of what happened, but in how the conflicts therein picked at the convictions of its actors raw.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I wasn't expecting the Screaming Phoenix Killer to die at this point, but it was a really impressive exchange that said a lot about who he was in the end. And further about Betsu Ten Gai and Rin Setsu. Shu Un's lessons to Ken and Shou Fu Kan's response to Tan Hi's lamentation were also interesting to see. That's really what this episode was about, pushing the blade of circumstance under these characters' skins to show us some what makes them different.<br /> <br /> And coming up, seems we might finally learn why Shou Fu Kan's title is the Edgeless Blade, if our legendary thief's reaction to seeing his weapon up close and the man himself breaking in to even the score is any indication.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It occurs to me that in the opening, as opposed to Mu Sho cleanly splitting a petal in two with a swing of his sword, Fu Kan seems to simply strike through one so hard with his sword that he pulverizes it outright.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 09-02-2016, 07:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T06:34:35-07:00","id":962794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/951376-exalted-related-media-thunderbolt-fantasy-aka-exalted-the-tv-show?p=962564#post962564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was a pretty brutal episode, not just in terms of what happened, but in how the conflicts therein picked at the convictions of its actors raw.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I wasn't expecting the Screaming Phoenix Killer to die at this point, but it was a really impressive exchange that said a lot about who he was in the end. And further about Betsu Ten Gai and Rin Setsu. Shu Un's lessons to Ken and Shou Fu Kan's response to Tan Hi's lamentation were also interesting to see. That's really what this episode was about, pushing the blade of circumstance under these characters' skins to show us some what makes them different.<br /> <br /> And coming up, seems we might finally learn why Shou Fu Kan's title is the Edgeless Blade, if our legendary thief's reaction to seeing his weapon up close and the man himself breaking in to even the score is any indication.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It occurs to me that in the opening, as opposed to Mu Sho cleanly splitting a petal in two with a swing of his sword, Fu Kan seems to simply strike through one so hard with his sword that he pulverizes it outright.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly I thought you were referencing episode 8, so I opened the spoiler of episode 9. That was an intense episode, for sure.<br /> <br /> So what's up with Shang? He got dumped on pretty heavily by the group, but he's the only one we've seen fight with his fists, he's cracked steel and healed wounds with his ki. No one else has performed feats quite like he has. Is that a setting conceit or are we looking at something special here?<br /> <br /> Didn't notice he obliterated the falling petal. Badass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T10:23:12-07:00","id":962877,"title":"","content":"Unfortunate, that.<br /> <br /> I'm fairly sure that his feats are extensions of whatever martial training he's had (which is apparently not suited for fighting with a regular sword), as opposed to things like Xing Hai's necromancy and Mie Tian Hai's mentioned dread powers. Like the Meteor Walking demonstrated by various characters and Mie Tian Hai's occasional mind over matter swordfighting, Shang's lay on hands healing and steel cracking move are still mostly mortal skills, not spells. So they're not inherently unusual as far as the setting goes, but they're obviously impressive (and the seeming versatility of his skill with ki seems special).<br /> <br /> The setting conceit at play is how martial arts include esoteric and weird techniques, but aren't blatantly supernatural or dispensers of miracle-like effects because those are the wheelhouse of sorcery and its kind. This is common to Wuxia, and you can see it in how Martial Arts and Sorcery were written for Ex3 to an extent as well.<br /> <br /> Some of the feats in Thunderbolt Fantasy blur the distinction a bit (several of Dan Fei's anti-evil techniques seem like part of her family style but are also treated like spells, and Xing Hai laying the dead of the valley to rest was as much of a performance relying on emotion and familiarity as it was a magical ritual).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 09-03-2016, 02:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T15:50:22-07:00","id":962987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/951376-exalted-related-media-thunderbolt-fantasy-aka-exalted-the-tv-show?p=962564#post962564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">And coming up, seems we might finally learn why Shou Fu Kan's title is the Edgeless Blade, if our legendary thief's reaction to seeing his weapon up close and the man himself breaking in to even the score is any indication.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Considering all he has done in this series, he probably is some monk, used to fight without sharp weapon (staff, maybe?). Second thing - his entire character makes me constantly think about one other classical anime character - <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Hitokiri Battousai</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew/rewrites:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882274-new-spell-and-some-2nd-edition-spells-rewrite-for-3rd-edition-peach\" target=\"_blank\">2nd-&gt;3rd Edition Sorcery Spells Rewrite</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=890192#post890192\" target=\"_blank\">Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes Evocations</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/913443-occult-sorcery-charms-homebrew-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Occult Charms for Sorcerers</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/903155-peach-solar-thrown-charms-for-different-fighting-style-11-charms\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Thrown Charms (with Solar Danmaku Charms)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11704-daerian","name":"Daerian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T05:27:58-07:00","id":966155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Growls</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/951376-exalted-related-media-thunderbolt-fantasy-aka-exalted-the-tv-show#post951376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We all knew that there was a bunch of badass puppeteers in Taiwan, of the non-hopping kind.<br /> They've been doing amazing work for the last several decades, making wuxia-puppetry. Now, Gen Urobuchi of<i> Fate/Zero</i> and <i>Puella Magi Madoka Magica </i>fame decided to work with the crowning jewel of that industry, to create a Puppet show for a new audience.<br /> <br /> AND IT IS GLORIOUS.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is ... is that TM Revolution I hear?<br /> <br /> Fukkin <i>sold</i>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:courier\">REALITY.SYS corrupt. Reboot Universe? Y/N/Q</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/230-taichara","name":"taichara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar230_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T13:37:59-07:00","id":966413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>taichara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/951376-exalted-related-media-thunderbolt-fantasy-aka-exalted-the-tv-show?p=966155#post966155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is ... is that TM Revolution I hear?<br /> <br /> Fukkin <i>sold</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why YES, good sir-and/or-madam, it is! <br /> <br /> In other news, episode 10! Good stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T16:12:06-07:00","id":975262,"title":"","content":"This week's was one heck of an episode as far as the prelude to a finale goes. So many things came to a head just in time for the climax of the story. Shang was freaking amazing. And at the very end, Lin Xue Ya... I thought he couldn't pull another one like this on us. I was wrong.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">There were a lot of conflicts and character themes that reached a clear culmination in this episode. We finally understood Mie Tian Hai's defining ethos, Shang's real power and his character, and Xing Hai's true objective in the midst of this adventure. In the events that ensued, the remaining veils in the story of the Tian Xing Jian were pulled away. And in a conclusion that spanned the episode, the idea that what really matters is one's skill and not your weapons, that how a person uses what they have and wield the truth of what they are, are what defines a hero.<br /> <br /> And of course, it was a wonderful climax for the thought expressed in Lin Xua Ya's soliloquy. That the most important truths are sometimes hidden so well they may as well be in plain sight.<br /> <br /> After we had it revealed that his way as a knave was that of a legendary thief whose feats were the product of his recognizable wits, I didn't think there was another layer of that plain and yet surprising magnitude that he could pull back to surprise us. Even when Mien Tian Hai seemed to have by all rights outsmarted him, he looked about ready to cook up more bullshit that would somehow turn things to his advantage. Instead he flabbergasted expectations by confirming an early suspicion many had likely <i>dismissed because we mistook the revelation of the canny thief</i> <i>for the entire truth</i>, despite existing hints to the contrary. And with it, turning Mien Tian Hai's take on his soliloquy - his stance of having no desire to show his swordsmanship, preferring to keep it concealed and only use it when necessary - back at him.<br /> <br /> Bite me if that is not how you do an awesome tricksy Sidereal ally.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">(Or it could be another hallucination, since he was messing with the pipe, but I doubt it at this point.)</span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> All in all, an incredible showing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 09-24-2016, 08:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T09:43:07-07:00","id":979116,"title":"","content":"We will get more!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2016-09-30/gen-urobuchi-thunderbolt-fantasy-puppet-series-gets-sequel/.107092\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/thumbnails/crop600x315gDF/cms/news/103085/puppets.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2016-09-30/gen-urobuchi-thunderbolt-fantasy-puppet-series-gets-sequel/.107092\" target=\"_blank\"> Gen Urobuchi's Thunderbolt Fantasy Puppet Series Gets Sequel </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2016-09-30/gen-urobuchi-thunderbolt-fantasy-puppet-series-gets-sequel/.107092\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2016-09-30/gen-urobuchi-thunderbolt-fantasy-puppet-series-gets-sequel/.107092 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Japanese/Taiwanese co-production ended on Friday // The 13th and final episode of the \"chivalrous fantasy puppet show\" Thunderbolt Fantasy ended on Friday... </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T12:40:50-07:00","id":979209,"title":"","content":"This ending episode was near-perfect. The series had gripping pacing since the first episode, and I'm impressed by how it always kept something about the characters to reveal, often in reinforcement of its themes. The show had interesting things to say about conflict and the pursuit of power, but best of all was the underlying irony of the circumstances that questioned those ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 09-30-2016, 04:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T03:19:53-07:00","id":979568,"title":"","content":"It was a bit of a deus ex machina unfortunately, and I felt like it was rushed. As far as an &quot;anime&quot; ending goes, it didn't suck, which most anime I see have AWFUL endings (Soul Eater and Gundam Seed jump to my mind at the moment). 8.5/10 ending, 9.5/10 for the overall series.<br /> <br /> Those anima banners yo. This is Exalted, straight up.<br /> <br /> Edit: *chanting* Sequel! Sequel!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T04:42:26-07:00","id":979590,"title":"","content":"That is about my only gripe with it. A forgivable, but significant one. In contrast to everything else that was amazing about him, Shang's final solution effectively came out of nowhere, though it added some detail to his motives and set up future conflicts nicely.<br /> <br /> The real epic clash of the finale was a super Exalted battle though. And soaked in brutal philosophical questioning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 10-01-2016, 07:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T07:43:38-07:00","id":979651,"title":"","content":"Right, Enigmatic Gale got the real finale, -and our main character got a (cool) deus ex machina power. Good, but it could have been better. No foreshadowing of the power makes it seem like a ridiculous plot twist.<br /> <br /> Still loved it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T08:14:26-07:00","id":979669,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I love how salty Lin Xue Ya got too after breaking Mien Tian Hai's pride made the latter snap back with extreme prejudice. Got the last laugh after all.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 10-01-2016, 11:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T01:15:53-07:00","id":984781,"title":"","content":"At this point, Shang reminds me more of Dugu Qiubai, &quot;lonely, begging defeat&quot; than anyone else.<br /> <br /> Also, yes, he basically pulled those swords out of his ass but I found the performance and script made up for it because I imagined a used car salesman tone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11538-kingcrackers","name":"kingcrackers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11538_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T15:54:28-07:00","id":1082416,"title":"","content":"I know this thread is old but I have to put in my two cents. I am on episode seven and I have to say this show is GLORIOUS! I want my next exalted Chronicle to be as rich and dramatic as this show.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>May you live in interesting times...</i><br /> <br /> Storyteller of <b><a href=\"https://sunforgedoath.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Sun Forged Oath</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1998-keichiokami","name":"Keichiokami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1998_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T16:55:46-07:00","id":1082439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Keichiokami</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/951376-exalted-related-media-thunderbolt-fantasy-aka-exalted-the-tv-show?p=1082416#post1082416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know this thread is old but I have to put in my two cents. I am on episode seven and I have to say this show is GLORIOUS! I want my next exalted Chronicle to be as rich and dramatic as this show.</div> </div> </div> </div>Truth be told, I based my own Exalted Chronicle off of it. Suffice to say, it helps to have a confederate in your Circle if you want to play around with the same kind of space as Phantom Bird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Need some Tunes for your Exalted Game? <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1071249-exalted-tunes\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-exalted-tunes</a><br /> Want some help managing your PCs? <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882498-new-anathema-character-management-anathema-reincarnated\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...a-reincarnated</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2442-arian-dynas","name":"Arian Dynas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T20:19:11-07:00","id":1082498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arian Dynas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/951376-exalted-related-media-thunderbolt-fantasy-aka-exalted-the-tv-show?p=1082439#post1082439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Truth be told, I based my own Exalted Chronicle off of it. Suffice to say, it helps to have a confederate in your Circle if you want to play around with the same kind of space as Phantom Bird.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Arian I have you to thank you getting into this show full throttle. You mentioned it in the &quot;What game are you running?&quot; thread and I was reminded about it. I looked it up again on crunchyroll and I am hooked.<br /> <br /> I hear you on Phantom Bird, but he sure reminds me of many a sidereal NPC I have played to guide the plot. I played a reoccuring Sidereal NPC named Daisuki Dan who was a Calinti Spy/Court Performer who was a lot like Phantom Bird. That character is truly a great inspiration for how Sidereals maybe be portrayed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>May you live in interesting times...</i><br /> <br /> Storyteller of <b><a href=\"https://sunforgedoath.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Sun Forged Oath</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1998-keichiokami","name":"Keichiokami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1998_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T21:29:03-07:00","id":1082513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Keichiokami</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/951376-exalted-related-media-thunderbolt-fantasy-aka-exalted-the-tv-show?p=1082498#post1082498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Arian I have you to thank you getting into this show full throttle. You mentioned it in the &quot;What game are you running?&quot; thread and I was reminded about it. I looked it up again on crunchyroll and I am hooked.<br /> <br /> I hear you on Phantom Bird, but he sure reminds me of many a sidereal NPC I have played to guide the plot. I played a reoccuring Sidereal NPC named Daisuki Dan who was a Calinti Spy/Court Performer who was a lot like Phantom Bird. That character is truly a great inspiration for how Sidereals maybe be portrayed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh to clarify; my &quot;Phantom Bird&quot; Onyx Silk Wind, Servant of the Starmetal Garden is one of my players. He and I had hatched this plot for MONTHS before hand. And not a single one of my PCs figured it out until the last moment. The looks on all their faces was worth all the trouble up to that point.<br /> <br /> Prior to that I'd used several characters to draw them together; Brilliant Owl, Resplendent Destiny of the Treasure Trove, Tiger Eye, Resplendent Destiny of the Spear, Peleps Hisakawa D. Junko, whom it's still out on whether or not he's a Resplendent Destiny or not. I'll keep my PCs guessing, Honest Hamul, Resplendent Destiny of the Key. And of course, Rust-Eyes, the most depressing man on Earth, Resplendent Destiny of the Sword.<br /> <br /> There were so many times my player was sure I was giving it away, straight up telling them, but when the players looked back, they realized, none of these characters were ever in the same place, except Junko; some'd even figured out that there was a Sidereal about, but none of them ever suspected poor Rust Eyes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Need some Tunes for your Exalted Game? <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1071249-exalted-tunes\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-exalted-tunes</a><br /> Want some help managing your PCs? <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882498-new-anathema-character-management-anathema-reincarnated\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...a-reincarnated</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2442-arian-dynas","name":"Arian Dynas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T03:32:31-07:00","id":1082553,"title":"","content":"Sounds great!<br /> I'm gonna check it out. Thanks for showing it, Growls!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1920-kim","name":"Kim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T15:27:22-07:00","id":1083719,"title":"","content":"You're welcome.<br /> <br /> Also, to the interested, there's a second season in production, as well as a prequel 1.5 hour special about Sha Wu Sheng and his past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>__________________________________________________ </b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><i>Preaching the enlightened gospels of Gaming Anarchy</i></b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/225-growls","name":"Growls","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T15:48:15-07:00","id":1083726,"title":"","content":"Any word on expect air dates and such?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T15:59:39-07:00","id":1083734,"title":"","content":"The second season would be 2018. 1.5 years of turnaround seems about right","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>__________________________________________________ </b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><i>Preaching the enlightened gospels of Gaming Anarchy</i></b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/225-growls","name":"Growls","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:"